# Java Method Signature and Block Layout

When writing or editing Java methods:

## Method signature

- Write the full method signature on **one line** (modifiers, return type, name, parameters).
- Put the opening brace `{` on the **same line** as the signature.
- Put the closing brace `}` on its **own line** after the body.

```java
public String temp(String a, String b) {

}
```

## Line breaks inside the method

- Between statements of the **same kind** (same role or repeated pattern): **one** line break only — no blank line.
- Between blocks with **different meaning** (e.g. setup vs validation vs return): insert **one blank line** before the next block.

## Braces for blocks

For `if`, `for`, `try`, lambdas with blocks, etc.:

- Write the controlling line first, then `{`, then a line break, then the body, then `}` on its own line.

```java
public String example(String error, Model model) {

    model.addAttribute("screenName", "관리자 로그인");
    model.addAttribute("purpose", "관리자 인증을 수행합니다.");

    if (error != null) {
        model.addAttribute("loginError", "아이디 또는 비밀번호가 올바르지 않습니다.");
    }

    return "admin/auth/login";
}
```

Do not split a method signature across multiple lines unless that file already does so and you are making a minimal surgical edit.

## Java `record` types

- **Not** subject to the one-line method signature rule above.
- Follow `.cursor/rules/java-record-schema.mdc` for component spacing and `@Schema` annotations.
